  "id": "Compound::DB00808 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "Indapamide is likely to interact with Ca9 through a series of molecular and cellular mechanisms involving Ca4 and Ca12. The evidence suggests that Indapamide binds to Ca4, which then participates in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, an activity that is also associated with Carbonate Dehydratase Activity. This pathway is ultimately linked to Ca9, indicating a potential role in the cellular processes of Ca9. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Indapamide influences the function of Ca9, possibly through modulation of calcium-related biochemical processes. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Indapamide to Ca9 underscores the complexity of the interaction, suggesting that Indapamide may exert its effects through a network of biochemical interactions involving calcium-dependent enzymes.",
